#! /bin/bash
#
# tools/check_write_surface — CI guard for ADR 0027
# (CoreActionController is the single GUI->engine write surface).
#
# Fails if GUI code (src/gui/src) calls a *mutating* method directly on an
# engine-owned core (Basics) object instead of routing the edit through
# CoreActionController. This is the "done-when" gate for the Phase 4.5
# write-surface sweep (proposal 0005).
#
# Scope: (1) direct mutation of engine-owned **Basics** objects (Note, Pattern,
# Playlist, Instrument, InstrumentComponent, InstrumentLayer, Sample, Adsr,
# Song, Drumkit, AutomationPath) via the conventional pointer names; (2) direct
# mutation / playback commands on AudioEngine / Transport / Sampler
# (set*/reset*/... and noteOn/noteOff/previewInstrument/stopPlayingNotes).
#
# NOT enforced (by design): state *reads* under a hand-rolled lock() — e.g. the
# SongEditor position ruler / pattern list reading transport & playing-pattern
# state for painting, and the SampleEditor's editor-local preview-instrument
# mutation. These are not song-graph writes; in editor mode they become telemetry
# reads (ADR 0018), a separate migration. The few preview/audition calls that
# play an editor-local or not-yet-in-song object through the sampler are
# allowlisted below, pending the editor-mode preview design (ADR 0016).
#
# Legitimate exceptions (ADR 0027 buckets C/D, editor-local working copies,
# scratch/preview notes, file & session bookkeeping) are listed in ALLOW with a
# reason. Prefer routing through CoreActionController over adding an entry here.
#
# Copyright(c) 2008-2026 The hydrogen development team [hydrogen-devel@lists.sourceforge.net]
#
# http://www.hydrogen-music.org
#
